// ============================================================================
// scint_pol.kn — TurboKain 17: Interstellar Scintillation & Polarization Coherence
// (Objective 1: ISM diffractive scattering vs local backend wander, I2 -> I3 grade)
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS:
// A celestial point source shines THROUGH the turbulent interstellar medium (ISM),
// and the medium imprints physical signatures no local generator can fake:
//
//   1. Diffractive Scintillation: Scattering modulates intensity (modulation
//      index m ~ 0.2 - 1.0, timescale tau >= 2 frames), DECORRELATED across
//      frequency sub-bands (xcorr < 0.80). Terrestrial hum is steady (m ~ 0.06);
//      local RFI bursts are broadband-simultaneous (xcorr ~ 0.95+, COMMON).
//   2. Polarization Coherence: A celestial signal arrives in every feed at the
//      SAME frequency (dfreq <= 3 bins) or with locked sky-time envelope
//      co-variation (env_xcorr > 0.50). The known-local HIP-113357 receiver
//      wander fingerprint is the opposite: each polarization drifts to a
//      different frequency (WANDER-LOCAL).
//
// Hit Criteria Role:
// This instrument provides the exact astrophysical proof that promotes an
// engineered candidate from I2 (ENGINEERED) to I3 (INTERSTELLAR-LEAN).
//
// Contract: .f32 (pol0) + optional .f32 (pol1) -> scint.md + scint.csv
// Exit codes: 0 searched, 1 help OR prove fail, 2 error.
// ============================================================================

